180HF c  No |b{+-} population (0.005% {I18}) from {+180}Lu to {+180m}Hf(5.5 h)  
180HF2c  (1986Ke19). Other value: 0.46% {I15} (1984Es02). The discrepancy with  
180HF3c  the value given by 1986Ke19 could be explained by assuming the         
180HF4c  existence of a {+180}Lu isomer. However, 1986Le19 found no evidence    
180HF5c  of a {+180}Lu isomer in the 10-300 s half-life range. % branching      
180HF6c  given by 1984Es02 may be affected by an imprecise correction of the    
180HF7c  contribution from {+180}Hf (5.5 h) directly produced in the reaction.  
180HF8c  Its uncertainty may have also been underestimated by using a linear    
180HF9c  approximation with partial derivatives for the propagation of large    
180HFac  uncertainties.                                                         
